  "anomaly_detected": true,
  "confidence": 0.55,
  "anomalies": [
    {
      "category": "other",
      "components": ["R6", "R9"],
      "pins": ["R6.1", "R6.2", "R9.1", "R9.2"],
      "nets": ["FLOAT_HIGH", "FLOAT_LOW"],
      "observed": "In the 'Water Level Sensor/Switches' block, R6 (10 kΩ) is tied between +3V3 and the FLOAT_HIGH node (J1 pin 2 'HIGH'), and R9 (10 kΩ) is tied between GND and the FLOAT_LOW node (J1 pin 3 'LOW'). Thus FLOAT_HIGH is pulled up and FLOAT_LOW is pulled down.",
      "expected": "The specification's netlist states the opposite biasing: 'R6 FLOAT_LOW +3V3 10k, R9 GND FLOAT_HIGH 10k' — i.e. FLOAT_LOW should carry the +3V3 pull-up (R6) and FLOAT_HIGH should carry the pull-down to GND (R9). The two pull resistors are connected to the wrong float nets, inverting the idle logic of both float switches.",
      "evidence": [
        {"source": "schematic", "quote": "Water Level Sensor/Switches / Safety Switches: +3V3 → R6 10k → node → FLOAT_HIGH; R9 10k → GND on node → FLOAT_LOW (J1 pins 2/3 = HIGH/LOW)"},
        {"source": "spec", "quote": "§4.4: 'the netlist's FLOAT_LOW/FLOAT_HIGH nets (with 10 kΩ/4.7 kΩ pull resistors visible in the .cir file: R6 FLOAT_LOW +3V3 10k, R9 GND FLOAT_HIGH 10k, R2 FLOAT_LOW /BPUMP 4.7k, R11 FLOAT_HIGH /BATO 4.7k).'"}
      ],
      "impact": "The pull-up/pull-down assignment of the two float-switch inputs is swapped relative to the intended design. This inverts the idle (de-energised) state seen by ESP32 IO0/IO1 and, because R2 (4k7, FLOAT_LOW) feeds the main-pump interlock transistor T1 and R11 (4k7, FLOAT_HIGH) feeds the ATO-valve interlock transistor T4, it also reverses the default state of the low-level pump cutoff and high-level overflow interlocks, so the safety logic behaves opposite to what was intended.",
      "confidence": 0.55
    }
  ],
  "summary": "Most of the schematic matches the specification (power train, ADM3260 isolated pH/EC channels, TMC2209 drivers with 110 mΩ sense and 14 k/10 k7 VREF dividers, 2.2 k I2C pull-ups, DNP LiDAR/BME280/BH1750). The one deviation is that the FLOAT_HIGH/FLOAT_LOW pull resistors R6 and R9 are attached to the opposite nets from the spec's netlist, swapping the pull-up/pull-down biasing of the two float switches and inverting the float-interlock logic."
}

